    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0140" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.6215/24: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-31T23:00:00+03:00">January 31,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 31—8:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>199. Embassy’s 652, September 29, 5 p.m. 1939<anchor n="30" xml:id="d125-f1"/> A
                    communiqué published in today’s newspapers announces the exchange yesterday by
                    Molotov and the German Ambassador<anchor n="31" xml:id="d125-f2"/> of the
                    instruments of ratification of the agreement concerning juridical relations
                    along the frontier signed August 31, 1940 and of the “protocols and other
                    documents <pb facs="0141" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/> relating to this agreement”,
                    adding that the agreement is based on the treaty of September 28, 1939
                    concerning friendship and the boundary between the Soviet Union and
                        Germany,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d125-f3"/> and that it was ratified by the
                    Soviet and German Governments December 5, 1940, on which date it entered into
                    effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d125-f1" n="30" xml:id="d125-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see telegram No. 1472, September 29, 1939, from The Chargé in
                    Germany, <ref target="frus1939v01#pg_481">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1939, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 481</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f2" n="31" xml:id="d125-f2-content">
                <p>Friedrich Werner, Count von der Schulenburg.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d125-f3" n="32" xml:id="d125-f3-content">
                <p>Signed in Moscow; for text, see <hi rendition="#italic">Nazi-Soviet Relations,
                        1939–1941</hi>, p. 105; or <hi rendition="#italic">Documents on German
                        Foreign Policy, 1918–1945</hi>, Series D, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >viii</hi>, p. 164.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
